From a639c5602e1889e478f6888fc1a781ef9405ed30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:48:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: type peer protocol rejection and lifecycle
 diagnostics

Convert 47 existing peer-message, request rejection, disconnect, Avalanche
and stalling-timeout producers with existing typed fields. Preserve message
text, severity/category, sanitization and all protocol/state/penalty behavior.
Numeric peer IDs, versions, counts and seconds retain their actual domains;
exception details use existing bounded copied Error fields. No new fields,
producer API, tests, rule catalogs or framework machinery.

The exact mechanical script below uses the existing AST converter and its
severity/message validation. Regex is not used to find C++ source boundaries.
Reviewed the resulting diff; scoped lint checks 100 production events and
git diff --check passes. Compilation/runtime tests: NOT RUN. Validate once
in the final canonical native cohort rather than compiling each conversion.

Scripted-diff commands (run at this commit parent):
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python - <<'PY'
